<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Polynesians</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Polynesians are the peoples of the islands within the Polynesian triangle of the central and southern Pacific, from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaii</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/easter-island">Easter Island</a>. Descended from Austronesian seafarers of the Lapita culture, they reached Tonga and Samoa around 900–800 BCE and later settled the remote islands in long canoe voyages guided by stars, winds and swells. They share related languages and traditions of chiefly rank.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/polynesians.jpg" alt="Polynesians" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original uploader was Ciell at nl.wikipedia · CC BY-SA 2.5 nl · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maori_welkom.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
